      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Natural Vegetation"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Tropical Deciduous Forests are the most widespread forest type in India, commonly known as Monsoon Forests.",
        "Tropical Evergreen Forests thrive in regions with heavy annual rainfall exceeding 200 cm and high humidity.",
        "Thorn Forests and Scrubs develop in arid and semi-arid regions receiving less than 70 cm of rainfall.",
        "Montane forests exhibit a distinct succession of vegetation types corresponding to elevation and temperature changes.",
        "Mangrove forests are specialized coastal ecosystems situated along river deltas, dominated by salt-tolerant species like Sundari trees."
      ],
      "id": "q4v62dj"
